# Regression (QA M0): holding JUMP through the death and respawn must not
# make the player jump without a new press.
# Steps: fall into the 3-wide gap (Died at 235), press and hold JUMP from step
# 236 (during Dying) with RIGHT+RUN; respawn at 295.
# Expected: Game tracks jump_held while Dying and keeps it on respawn, so the
# player just runs along the ground: x~76.9 at step 325 (same as without JUMP).
# Was: Jumped at step 296 (Player::spawn reset jump_held, so the held button
# counted as a fresh press) and x=64 at step 325.
level  = testbed
seed   = 1
source = handwritten
expect = dies_at frames=235..235 deaths=1 state=playing player_x>=76
---
RB 110
RBJ 35
RB 90     # runs off into the 3-wide gap, Died at 235
RBJ 90    # JUMP pressed during Dying and held through the respawn (295)
